  "design_notes": {
    "overall_style": "Swiss-influenced minimalist editorial motion graphics on the Night Depth navy gradient. White type, with Steel Teal used only for the one chosen customer and the key word.",
    "type_size": "Headlines are 44–56px on a 1080px-wide frame, with a 72% max width, so there is always generous navy space around the words. Nothing goes above 56px.",
    "pacing": "Each scene holds for at least 3 seconds (the last one holds for about 2 seconds after the text lands). Entrances run 400–700ms, then the frame rests. Only one thing moves at a time: text first, then the grid. Scenes are joined with soft 250–300ms cross-fades instead of hard cuts.",
    "motion_language": "Calm and purposeful. No bounce or snap. Every motion reinforces the message.",
    "grid_motif": "The 3x3 grid is an audience of nine people. It goes from floating cards → all nine fade out (talking to everyone) → 3D isometric with one cell lifting → flat 2D with one teal cell → that cell pops → the other eight drift away.",
